-- הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד מיום 15.8.1982 בדבר שאילת והשאלת מורים בבתי-ספר
-- על-יסודיים שש-שנתיים: the State (side A, the employer of the teachers of
-- grades 7–9), the Centre of Local Government and the three large cities
-- (side B, the employers of grades 10–12) and the two teachers' unions agree
-- that a teacher who teaches in both divisions of a six-year school is
-- employed by one employer only — the "lending employer" — who lends him to
-- the other for the hours he teaches there. Registered on 15.11.1982 (no.
-- 7072/82). The schools (§2, annex א'); the lending employer, by tenure,
-- seniority and hours (§4); the lent teacher's rights (§5); the lending
-- and the reckoning between the employers (§6, annex ב'); the letter of
-- consent (§7, annex ג'); teachers without tenure (§8); commencement and
-- the end of the salary-merging agreement of 4.2.1975 (§9); a special
-- committee, disputes and joining (§§10–12, annex ד').
--
-- It speaks to no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is in no root.
-- What it cites outside itself — the salary-merging agreement of 4.2.1975,
-- the stay-hours agreement of the director-general's circular of 26.5.1981
-- and the salaries booklet — is a named input where a rule needs it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT conventions

-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §5 makes the lent teacher
-- the lending employer's employee for all purposes, his severance (or
-- pension) among them, and annex ב' §7 has a joint committee decide claims
-- beyond what the law gives; neither computes severance, takes any of it
-- away or puts a fund payment in its place, so they rule nothing the law
-- puts a floor under.

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: the lent teacher's
-- hours are divided between the two employers by the share of his
-- position with each, and his stay hours are paid by the stay-hours
-- agreement (annex ב' §5); shares of a position and pay, not a working
-- day or week.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: the word the search found is
-- ‘בעל תעודת זהות’ in the letter of consent the teacher signs; nothing
-- here gives pay or other remuneration by sex.

§ `הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — שאילת והשאלת מורים בבתי-ספר על-יסודיים שש-שנתיים (15.8.1982)`

DECLARE `1982 teacher-lending action` IS ONE OF
    `update the list of six-year schools`
    `employ the teacher in his whole position`
    `lend the teacher to the other employer for his hours there`
    `keep the trend of half his hours in the upper division`
    `sign the letter of consent`
    `try to place a teacher without tenure in one division only`
    `try to place a teacher without tenure at a third of a position in one division`
    `deal with the teachers the agreement finds no solution for`
    `convene the joint committee within a month`
    `ask the other employers to join the 1982 agreement`
    `draw up the yearly lists of lent teachers`
    `carry out the reckoning between the employers`
    `report the teachers' presence in the two divisions`

DECLARE `employer in a six-year school, of 1982` IS ONE OF
    `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`
    `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`

`why the agreements it cites are not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "הסכם איחוד המשכורות מיום 4.2.1975; הסכם שעות השהייה (חוזר מנכ\"ל מיוחד ה' תשמ\"א, שכפול/23, 26.5.1981); חוברת שכה\"ל"

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 A filing mark and a handwritten note; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 The registration stamp (15.11.1982, no. 7072/82), partly illegible, and a handwritten note; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 Side A: the State, by the wages commissioner and the Ministry of Education's director-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 Side B: the Centre of Local Government for the local authorities save the three large cities, and the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18 Side C: הסתדרות המורים and ארגון מורי בתי-הספר העל-יסודיים; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p25 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p26 Signatures at the foot of the page; no rule.

-- ¶7: made and signed in Jerusalem on 15.8.1982, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p7
`the teacher-lending agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 8 1982

-- ¶19–¶24: the recitals. Side A employs the teachers of the middle
-- division (grades 7–9) of a six-year school, side B those of the upper
-- division (10–12); the school is one pedagogic and administrative unit;
-- some teachers teach in both; the principal may place teachers in both,
-- as the school needs and with regard to the lending; and a teacher who
-- teaches in both is employed, on this agreement's terms, by one employer.
@ref akn:preamble/p19 akn:preamble/p20
GIVEN g IS A NUMBER @desc the grade, 7 to 12
GIVETH A `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`
DECIDE `the employer of a six-year school's class of grade` g IS
    IF g AT MOST 9 THEN `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`
    ELSE `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`

GIVEN e IS A `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `the party that is` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982` THEN `the State`
    WHEN `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982` THEN `the local authority or owning body`

#ASSERT `the employer of a six-year school's class of grade` 9 EQUALS `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`
#ASSERT `the employer of a six-year school's class of grade` 10 EQUALS `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`

@ref akn:preamble/p21 akn:preamble/p22 akn:preamble/p23 akn:preamble/p24
`a teacher in both divisions is employed by one employer` MEANS TRUE

§§ `1 תוקף המבוא והנספחים`

-- akn:art_1 The heading of §1.

@ref akn:art_1/p1
`the 1982 lending agreement's preamble and annexes are part of it` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2 בתי-הספר אליהם מתייחס ההסכם`

-- akn:art_2 The heading of §2.

-- ¶1: the agreement is about the six-year secondary schools on the list of
-- annex א'; ¶2: the Ministry updates it from time to time, as more open.
@ref akn:art_2/p1 akn:art_2/p2
GIVEN `on annex א's list as updated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1982 lending agreement reaches the school` `on annex א's list as updated` IF
    `on annex א's list as updated`

`updating the list of six-year schools` MEANS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MAY   `update the list of six-year schools`

§§ `3 הגדרות`

-- akn:art_3 The heading of §3.

-- "עובד קבוע": permanent as is accepted in the education system (an input);
-- "מעסיק משאיל": the employer who employs a teacher in his whole position,
-- as §4 says.
@ref akn:art_3/p1 akn:art_3/p2 akn:art_3/p3
`what makes a teacher permanent under the 1982 agreement` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "עובד קבוע כמקובל במערכת החינוך"

§§ `4 מדדים לקביעת מעסיק משאיל`

-- akn:art_4 The heading of §4.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-3 The headings of 4.1, 4.2 and 4.3.

-- 4.1: a teacher permanent with one of the two employers is entitled to be
-- employed by it in his whole position. 4.2.א: one permanent with both, by
-- the one that employed him first. 4.2.ב: one hired by both at the same
-- time, by the one he worked most of his hours for — over the last four
-- years before the determination, or since he started if fewer. 4.2.ג:
-- where that check finds the same position with both, or positions that
-- differ by no more than 10 percent, by the one he chooses. The 10 percent
-- is a difference of two position shares, so it is measured in percentage
-- points (convention position.points). Without tenure with either he has
-- no lending employer: §8.1 leaves him out.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_a akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_b akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_b/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_c
DECLARE `1982 lent teacher` HAS
    `permanent with the State`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `permanent with the local authority`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed first by`                                 IS A MAYBE `employer in a six-year school, of 1982` @desc NOTHING where both took him on at the same time
    `his position with the State over the years checked`           IS A NUMBER
    `his position with the local authority over the years checked` IS A NUMBER
    `his choice`                                        IS A `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`

GIVEN `years since he started` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the years 4.2.ב checks` `years since he started` IS
    min 4 `years since he started`

GIVEN `the one position` IS A NUMBER, `the other position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the positions are within 4.2.ג's 10 percent` `the one position` `the other position` IF
        `the one position` MINUS `the other position` AT MOST 0.1
    AND `the other position` MINUS `the one position` AT MOST 0.1

GIVEN t IS A `1982 lent teacher`
GIVETH A MAYBE `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`
DECIDE `the lending employer of` t IS
    IF t's `permanent with the State` AND t's `permanent with the local authority`
    THEN CONSIDER t's `employed first by`
         WHEN JUST e THEN JUST e
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF `the positions are within 4.2.ג's 10 percent` (t's `his position with the State over the years checked`) (t's `his position with the local authority over the years checked`)
             THEN JUST (t's `his choice`)
             ELSE IF t's `his position with the State over the years checked` GREATER THAN t's `his position with the local authority over the years checked`
                  THEN JUST `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`
                  ELSE JUST `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`
    ELSE IF t's `permanent with the State`
         THEN JUST `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`
         ELSE IF t's `permanent with the local authority`
              THEN JUST `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`
              ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `permanent with the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `permanent with the local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employed first by` IS A MAYBE `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`
      `with the State` IS A NUMBER
      `with the local authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `1982 lent teacher`
DECIDE `a 1982 lending example` `permanent with the State` `permanent with the local authority` `employed first by` `with the State` `with the local authority` IS
    `1982 lent teacher` WITH
        `permanent with the State`                          IS `permanent with the State`
        `permanent with the local authority`                IS `permanent with the local authority`
        `employed first by`                                 IS `employed first by`
        `his position with the State over the years checked`           IS `with the State`
        `his position with the local authority over the years checked` IS `with the local authority`
        `his choice`                                        IS `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`

#ASSERT `the lending employer of` (`a 1982 lending example` FALSE TRUE NOTHING 0.3 0.7) EQUALS JUST `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`
#ASSERT `the lending employer of` (`a 1982 lending example` TRUE TRUE (JUST `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`) 0.8 0.2) EQUALS JUST `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`
#ASSERT `the lending employer of` (`a 1982 lending example` TRUE TRUE NOTHING 0.3 0.7) EQUALS JUST `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982`
-- 55% against 45% is 10 points: his choice (here the State)
#ASSERT `the lending employer of` (`a 1982 lending example` TRUE TRUE NOTHING 0.45 0.55) EQUALS JUST `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982`
#ASSERT `the lending employer of` (`a 1982 lending example` FALSE FALSE NOTHING 0.5 0.5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the years 4.2.ב checks` 2 EQUALS 2 AND `the years 4.2.ב checks` 7 EQUALS 4

-- 4.3.א: once the lending employer is set, a change in his hours in either
-- division does not move it — so long as his hours in the lending
-- employer's classes stay at a third of a position or more where it is side
-- A, or at half of all his hours in the school or more where it is side B.
-- 4.3.ג: notwithstanding (א), side B stays the lending employer of a
-- permanent teacher whose upper-division hours fell below half for the
-- school's needs. Below those bounds otherwise, the agreement sets no new
-- employer: such a teacher is one §10's special committee deals with.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_a akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_c
GIVEN e IS A `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`
      `his hours in its classes, as a share of a full position` IS A NUMBER
      `his hours in its classes, as a share of all his hours in the school` IS A NUMBER
      `they fell for the school's needs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lending employer stays` e `his hours in its classes, as a share of a full position` `his hours in its classes, as a share of all his hours in the school` `they fell for the school's needs` IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982` THEN
        `his hours in its classes, as a share of a full position` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3
    WHEN `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982` THEN
            `his hours in its classes, as a share of all his hours in the school` AT LEAST 0.5
        OR  `they fell for the school's needs`

#ASSERT `the lending employer stays` `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982` 0.4 0.3 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the lending employer stays` `the State, for grades 7 to 9, of 1982` 0.3 0.9 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the lending employer stays` `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982` 0.4 0.4 FALSE
#ASSERT `the lending employer stays` `the local authority, for grades 10 to 12, of 1982` 0.4 0.4 TRUE

-- 4.3.ב: for a teacher whose lending employer is side B, the principal
-- keeps the trend of employing him in the upper division for half of all
-- his hours in the school.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_b
`keeping side B's teacher half in the upper division` MEANS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `keep the trend of half his hours in the upper division`

§§ `5 זכויות מורה מושאל`

-- akn:art_5 The heading of §5.

-- A teacher employed by the lending employer is its employee for every
-- purpose from the lending — his salary with all its components, his
-- severance (or pension) and all his social and professional rights.
@ref akn:art_5/p1
GIVEN e IS A `employer in a six-year school, of 1982`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `1982 teacher-lending action`
DECIDE `employing the lent teacher` e IS
    PARTY `the party that is` e
    MUST  `employ the teacher in his whole position`

