    PARTY `the party that is` e
    MUST  `lend the teacher to the other employer for his hours there`

-- 6.2: the employers reckon as annex ב' says; it is no concern of side C,
-- and delays or harms none of the teachers' rights here.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-2/p1 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p2
`the reckoning between the employers delays the teacher's rights` MEANS FALSE

-- 6.3: a change in the extent of the lending, or its end, is by agreement
-- of the two employers, with regard to the lending and the principal's
-- view, as the school needs.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3/p1
GIVEN `the State agrees` IS A BOOLEAN, `the local authority agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lending may be changed or ended` `the State agrees` `the local authority agrees` IF
    `the State agrees` AND `the local authority agrees`

§§ `7 כתב הסכמה`

-- akn:art_7 The heading of §7.

-- A teacher lent "as said in section [illegible] above" signs the letter of
-- consent of annex ג' as a condition of the agreement applying to him. The
-- section the corpus cannot read is not one the rule turns on: the teacher
-- lent is the one §§4–6 lend.
@ref akn:art_7/p1
GIVEN `signed the letter of consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1982 lending agreement applies to the lent teacher` `signed the letter of consent` IF
    `signed the letter of consent`

`signing the letter of consent` MEANS
